{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01VbkMvdi7pDjh1pvGc1C47Z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the task and implement it.\n\nThe task is to create `pkg/sys/terminal_test.go` with unit tests for `TerminalWidth`. Let me review the requirements:\n\n1. Test that TerminalWidth returns error for pipe read end FD\n2. Test that TerminalWidth returns error for pipe write end FD\n3. Test that TerminalWidth returns error for regular file FD\n4. Test that TerminalWidth doesn't panic for any valid non-terminal FD\n5. Use package sys_test and //go:build darwin || linux\n\nI have all the context I need from the provided source code. Let me write the test file.\n\n\nNow I'm looking at the test file structure from the existing tests—I need to match the copyright header, build tag, and test organization patterns. Since `TerminalWidth` takes an int file descriptor rather than an `*os.File`, I'll need to extract the FD from file objects using the `Fd()` method.\n\nI'm planning three test cases covering pipes (both read and write ends) and regular files, each verifying that the function returns an error for non-terminal descriptors without panicking. I'll write this as a clean test file following the established patterns.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":31078,"cache_read_input_tokens":16066,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":31078},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b3d77cc5-7afc-4be9-8fcd-d694cdb31957","uuid":"38d7e6b7-b234-4b88-9dd3-b1d64526e067"}
